    51	
    52	''MEASURED'' (the code seat, the field seat, and the lead's own read of `face-gate-server.ts`): the dial already runs Noise IK with the dialer's fresh static inside message one, so a dialer already proves itself before the gate sends its verdict. A holder of a candidate responder public key alone cannot test a captured message one (it needs the `es` Diffie-Hellman). The knock (`gateKnock`, an HMAC over the bundle digest, which hashes the whole public pin) tests offline for anyone holding the full candidate pin and an observed path. Any cheap pre-filter keyed on public pin material has that property, WireGuard's `mac1` included (paper section 5.4.4); a pinned dialer holds exactly the public pin, so no filter can tell it from an observer holding the same pin. A filter an observer lacks needs a client-held secret outside the pin, which changes the admission and pinning model.
    53	
    54	''MEASURED'': the knock also selects the gate. The dispatcher registers each Nexus and route at an exact `<route>/<knock>` path; a knock-less dial needs another clear selector or a trial decryption against every gate on a route, and each trial costs one X25519.
    55	
    56	''BUILT, a defect apart from the leak'': `handleUpgrade` in `packages/lararium-node/src/face-gate-server.ts` once sent the HTTP 101 before the gate decrypted message one, so a holder of a learned path read a 101 for any well-formed token. It now asks `FaceGate.preflight` first: a flight that decrypts under no bundle of the stood gate draws a destroyed socket and the refusal `flight-undecrypted`, before any 101. The preflight decrypts message one once and `accept` decrypts it once more, so the gate's API keeps its one shape. It moves no wire byte.
    57	
    58	''The lean'' (LEAD): the leak stands accepted and named; the knock stays; the 101 ordering stands repaired; a secret pre-filter waits on the operator, since it adds a credential to the pin.
